									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mateogun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005751); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7005751&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607801856" alt="Mateogun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7005751)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mateogun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005751); return false;" >Mateogun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607798443 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Dec 2020 18:40</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13928306/an-scp-plot-looking-for-feedback-and-greenlight">An scp plot, looking for feedback and greenlight</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843203">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong>Drama/Mistery</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong> A revenge plot, guy gets contained, escaped and is subsecuently killed, twist is he might not be anomalous at all and the people who capture him wants revenge on a very real very non-anomalous crime.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
Opening by stating that this scp is both consider neutralized and is under scrutiny to decide wether he was or not anomalous. It describes an anomalous human with the ability to control people's mind if some specific requirements are met. Captured by an agent close to one of his victims(who was assaulted and killed by the SCP).The lead Researcher, a psychiatrist, allegedly gets controlled and helps the SCP escape, who ends up running into an ambush of the Goc, who kill him on sight</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Ok,&nbsp;whats&nbsp;the&nbsp;twist?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;I&nbsp;see</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The reality would be very much non-anomalous, the SCP has no such mind control abilities, just a charismatic personality and some antisocial disorders that makes him use his charisma to lure and assault woman at bars, his last victim is a family member of both the agent and the psichiatrist, who, with some help of other staff members, plot to classify him as an SCP, use the cold mindset of the foundation to run &quot;quite unnecessarily painful&quot; experiments on him, then pretend to be on his side and help him &quot;escape&quot; to his death. After the failed escape attempt, the research team members would defect/be demoted/ be terminated and the idea of they being controlled would still hang in the air, being that the reason the scp file was not deleted as a non-anomalous thing</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Quite like the Murder on the Orient Express, a story where a lot of people plot to murder someone who killed a family member, with an SCP twist that shows that the foundation could very well be containing normal people if you make enough people believe someone has special powers.</p>
