<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong>: Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: SCP-5293 is a standard 1982 VHS-C video tape with no visible production date or producer, with the words &quot;Training Video&quot; written along its side.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: When inserted into a video home system(also known as a VHS for short) created in or after the year 1982 and played, a video similar to that of an industrial training tape will begin to play for an inconsistent timeframe which varies with each viewing. The topic that SCP-5293 covers also varies, with the use of low-quality animation style and bold white text to explain instructions the only consistency throughout all videos. However, the methods suggested by SCP-5293 consist of highly dangerous, irrational, and otherwise unethical procedures that would naturally have no beneficial effect on the topic being covered.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>: After the completion of the video, the topic covered by SCP-5293 will immediately take place. If the viewer completes the instructions provided by SCP-5293, one of two outcomes will take place:</p>
<p>- Any threats or disasters generated by SCP-5293 will cease.<br />
- The viewer will escape or survive until any threat or disaster generated by SCP-5293 ceases.</p>
<p>However, if the viewer fails to successfully execute the instructions covered by SCP-5293, they will be killed by the scenario created by SCP-5293.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: I apologize if this isn't the correct way to submit a greenlight request, this is a first for me</p>

