<p>Hello hello! Not an official critter, but I can still read and give opinions. And I have two things to say here.</p>
<p>First, and maybe less important, why would this be an SCP? Why would they need to contain it? As I see it, this doesn't exist and if it does then it can't be seen by anyone. Containment is impossible and by the same token unnecessary, at that point, right? It would not be a threat to 'the masquerade' as it were, as literally nobody can see it.</p>
<p>So next, I want to ask what sort of narrative you wanna pursue. I think the best one you could go for would probably be the various arguments within the Foundation about whether it should or should not be an SCP. Also might help to tone down the religion analogy a bit? I personally don't have anything against it, but it could be possible that some people might see it as problematic.</p>

